      "cultural_notes_vi": "Seoul taxi system: (1) 95%+ tài xế honest — chỉ minority scam tourists. Đa phần ở Myeongdong, Itaewon, Hongdae — areas đông tourist; (2) BAR LAW: tất cả taxi ở Hàn BẮT BUỘC accept card payment. Cash-only = vi phạm luật, có thể report; (3) Meter rates 2026 Seoul: base 4,800원 (first 1.6km), +100원 per 132m, +100원 per 30sec idle. Night surcharge (00:00-04:00): +20%. Outside-Seoul surcharge: +20%. Toll roads passed: customer pays. Highest legitimate rate: ~25-30,000원 cho ride 30km within Seoul; (4) Apps: KakaoTaxi (most common, có English), Tada (premium), Uber (limited). App rides có complaint button — easier dispute; (5) Hotline khiếu nại: 120 (Seoul Dasan call center, English support); 1330 (Korea Tourism, English/Chinese/Japanese). Mẹo phòng ngừa: (a) Always note plate number trước khi vào; (b) Open Naver Maps + start navigation đến destination — tài xế thấy bạn track route ít dare detour; (c) Use Kakao Taxi app — dispute proof tự động qua app; (d) Refuse 'special service' ('I'll show you scenic route', 'special tour rate') — these = scams; (e) Có thể tự pull up route bằng Naver + show driver: 'Naver에서는 이 길이라고 나와요' (Naver shows this route). Recovery sau scam: receipt + plate number + screenshot route → submit qua app or 120 hotline → refund usual trong 7-14 ngày.",
      "cultural_notes_en": "Seoul taxi system: (1) 95%+ of drivers are honest — only a minority scam tourists, mostly in Myeongdong, Itaewon, Hongdae (tourist-heavy areas); (2) THE LAW: all taxis in Korea MUST accept card payment. Cash-only is illegal and reportable; (3) meter rates 2026 Seoul: base ₩4,800 (first 1.6km), +₩100 per 132m, +₩100 per 30s idle. Night surcharge (00:00–04:00): +20%. Outside-Seoul surcharge: +20%. Toll roads: the customer pays. Highest legitimate fare: ~₩25–30,000 for a 30km ride within Seoul; (4) apps: KakaoTaxi (most common, has English), Tada (premium), Uber (limited). App rides have a complaint button — easier disputes; (5) complaint hotlines: 120 (Seoul Dasan call center, English support); 1330 (Korea Tourism, English/Chinese/Japanese). Prevention tips: (a) always note the plate number before getting in; (b) open Naver Maps + start navigation to the destination — drivers who see you tracking the route rarely dare to detour; (c) use the KakaoTaxi app — dispute proof is automatic via the app; (d) refuse a 'special service' ('I'll show you the scenic route', 'a special tour rate') — these are scams; (e) you can pull up the route on Naver + show the driver: 'Naver에서는 이 길이라고 나와요' (Naver shows this route). Recovery after a scam: receipt + plate number + route screenshot → submit via the app or the 120 hotline → refund usually in 7–14 days.",
      "tip_advice_vi": "5 chiến lược phòng tránh taxi scam ở Seoul: (1) USE APP (KakaoTaxi/Uber) — fixed price visible, complaint history, không bị refuse short rides. Avoid hailing street taxi nếu mới đến Hàn; (2) NOTE PLATE NUMBER khi vào — chụp ảnh plate trước khi sit down (5 giây habit). Hàn taxi plate format: 서울XX 1234 (Seoul) hoặc tỉnh khác. Tài xế thấy = đỡ defensive; (3) NAVIGATE YOURSELF — open Naver Maps + start navigation. Tài xế thấy phone screen tracking = ít dare detour. Nếu deviate: '이 방향이 맞아요?' (this direction right?); (4) WATCH METER — should be ON từ giây đầu, KHÔNG nên có 추가 buttons pressed (ngoài start). Note initial 4,800원 rate. Final fare = meter only (KHÔNG +random surcharges); (5) ASK RECEIPT — '영수증 주세요' — even if no dispute, tax record + insurance claim. Khi gặp dispute: (a) STAY CALM — argue calm hơn fast resolution; (b) USE EVIDENCE: meter screenshot, GPS history, plate number; (c) CALL 120 nếu serious — Seoul Dasan English service mediates với driver realtime; (d) PAY first then report — refusing pay = legal trouble; instead pay overcharged amount + dispute later qua hotline → refund. Sau dispute: report qua KakaoTaxi app (nếu app ride) → screenshot route + receipt → submit. Refund time 7-14 ngày. Driver gets warning + may lose license nếu repeat offender.",
      "tip_advice_en": "Five strategies to avoid a Seoul taxi scam: (1) USE THE APP (KakaoTaxi/Uber) — a fixed price is visible, complaint history exists, no refusing short rides. Avoid hailing a street taxi if you're new to Korea; (2) NOTE THE PLATE NUMBER when getting in — photograph it before sitting down (a 5-second habit). Korean taxi plate format: 서울XX 1234 (Seoul) or another province. A driver who sees this is less defensive; (3) NAVIGATE YOURSELF — open Naver Maps + start navigation. A driver who sees your tracking screen rarely dares to detour. If they deviate: '이 방향이 맞아요?' (is this the right direction?); (4) WATCH THE METER — it should be ON from the first second, with NO extra buttons pressed (beyond start). Note the initial ₩4,800 rate. The final fare = meter only (no random surcharges); (5) ASK FOR A RECEIPT — '영수증 주세요' — even with no dispute, it's a tax record + insurance proof. In a dispute: (a) STAY CALM — a calm argument resolves faster; (b) USE EVIDENCE: meter screenshot, GPS history, plate number; (c) CALL 120 if serious — Seoul Dasan English service mediates with the driver in real time; (d) PAY first, then report — refusing to pay = legal trouble; instead, pay the overcharged amount + dispute later via the hotline → refund. After the dispute: report via the KakaoTaxi app (if it was an app ride) → screenshot the route + receipt → submit. Refund in 7–14 days. The driver gets a warning + may lose their license if a repeat offender.",
